  - chemoinformatics

abstract: >
  Rationale: High-throughput MALDI-MS analyses produce extensive datasets daily.
  Each spectrum obtained from a complex mixture of oligosaccharides, generated
  through the enzymatic digestion of polymeric carbohydrates, can contain a vast
  amount of information requiring processing. Therefore, the availability of
  specialized informatics tools to facilitate data interpretation is essential.

  Methods: SugarMALDI is introduced as a cloud-based platform designed to support
  MALDI-MS interpretation of oligosaccharides. It enables the identification of
  both labeled and unlabeled oligosaccharides in complex MALDI-MS spectra,
  facilitates molecular formula assignment, and assesses candidate matches
  according to mass accuracy. Users can select from nine elemental monosaccharides
  available in the database, as well as define ionization adducts and chemical
  modifications, and modify parameters, allowing the software to be flexibly
  tailored to specific analytical contexts.

  Results: Designed for high-throughput workflows, the platform accelerates data
  processing while ensuring reliable interpretation. It was successfully validated
  using enzymatically digested standard plant gums, including arabinogalactan and
  galactomannan, as well as authentic watercolor samples, confirming its robustness
  and practical relevance. The average execution time was approximately two minutes
  per file, increasing proportionally with the number of selected monosaccharides.
  These results highlight the software's efficiency, adaptability, and suitability
  for diverse analytical applications.

  Conclusions: SugarMALDI provides assisted data interpretation tailored to the
  needs of glycobiologists and glycochemists. It supports structural and compositional
  characterization, enables polysaccharide identification, and delivers clear
  visual reporting of results, thereby streamlining analysis and enhancing the
  efficiency and reliability of glycomic investigations.

